    <section id="compare">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">Intent routing</p>
          <h2>Point at the work. Skip the handoff ritual.</h2>
          <p>The focused task says what to do; GitHub priority says how much compute to use.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-grid">
          <div class="compare-col before" data-reveal>
            <div class="lbl">Manual handoff</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Restate whether the job is implementation, CI repair, conflict resolution, or review feedback.</li>
              <li>Copy the issue, failing checks, or exact comments into a prompt.</li>
              <li>Find the task checkout and the agent session already working there.</li>
              <li>Choose an agent, model, and reasoning effort for this run.</li>
              <li>Repeat the same setup when the next signal lands.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="compare-col after" data-reveal style="transition-delay:80ms">
            <div class="lbl">With lazybox</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Focus the task—or select the exact review comments—and press <kbd>w w</kbd>.</li>
              <li>lazybox builds the implementation, fix-CI, conflict, or feedback brief.</li>
              <li>One relevant running agent gets it; otherwise your default starts in the task worktree.</li>
              <li>A <code>high</code> / <code>medium</code> / <code>low</code> label or <code>@</code> marker picks the configured model and effort at spawn.</li>
              <li>Use <kbd>w S</kbd> / <kbd>w M</kbd> / <kbd>w L</kbd> when you want to override the tier directly.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow" data-reveal>
          <span class="tag">GitHub-only handoff</span>
          <p>
            Put <code>@high</code> and <code>@lazybox codex</code> in an issue body.
            lazybox opens the issue worktree, maps <b>high</b> through Codex's configured
            tier to its model and reasoning arguments, and starts the implementation brief.
            The task, agent, and compute profile all come from GitHub—no TUI handoff required.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

